    <string name="updates_rollback">Roll back</string>
    <string name="updates_rollback_desc">Android will not install an older version over a newer one, so a rollback means uninstalling first. That erases your servers, which is what the backup is for.</string>
    <string name="updates_no_archived">No previous versions saved yet.</string>
    <string name="updates_use">Use</string>
    <string name="updates_rollback_title">Roll back to %1$s</string>
    <string name="updates_rollback_steps">Two steps.

1. Uninstall PocketSSH below. Your servers stay in the backup folder.
2. Then open %1$s in the folder %2$s with a file manager and install it — PocketSSH will be gone by then, so it cannot do this part for you.

Afterwards, point the reinstalled app at the same folder and your servers come back.</string>
    <string name="updates_rollback_no_backup">There is no backup in the folder. Rolling back now would lose your servers for good.</string>
    <string name="updates_step_uninstall">1. Uninstall</string>
