    <string name="updates_install_failed_detail">Install failed: %1$s</string>
    <string name="updates_rollback_with_helper">PocketSSH Recovery will do this: it uninstalls the current version and installs %1$s straight afterwards. Android confirms each of those two steps.\n\nYour servers stay in %2$s and come back when you point the reinstalled app at that folder.</string>
    <string name="updates_helper_pitch">Without the helper the second step cannot be a button — once PocketSSH is uninstalled there is nothing left to press, so you would have to open the APK from your folder by hand.</string>
    <string name="updates_rollback_now">Roll back now</string>
    <string name="updates_install_helper">Install the helper</string>
    <string name="updates_helper_needs_check">Check for updates first so the helper can be downloaded.</string>
    <string name="updates_rollback_direct">Installing this version over the current one keeps every server and setting. Android will ask you to confirm once.</string>
    <string name="updates_rollback_via_helper">Roll back with the helper (uninstalls first)</string>
    <string name="updates_versions_desc">Every published version. Ones saved in your folder install without a network; the rest are downloaded when you pick them. Version codes are frozen, so moving in either direction keeps all your servers and settings.</string>
